-- Tests of §21 of the Oz LaTmura agreement of 14.8.2011 against the Hours
-- of Work and Rest Law (MMS-678; the card trip-units-overtime). For a
-- teacher under the reform in full its table, in place of §4.ד of the
-- agreement of 8.9.1998, pays 4 units for a day out ending between 21:00
-- and 24:00 and 6 for each night away, each 0.7% of the monthly combined
-- salary (§4.ג of that agreement, which it keeps). Measured against what the
-- law asks for the worked days (l4/lib/escort-day.l4), at the bound most
-- generous to the employer (convention instruments.regular-hour-wage): the
-- units fall short on the day out to 23:00, and on the night away even with
-- the night left out.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `escort-day`
IMPORT `oz-founding-21`

§ `בדיקות סעיף 21 להסכם עוז לתמורה מול חוק שעות עבודה ומנוחה`

GIVEN a IS AN `Oz out-of-school activity`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `regular hours section 21's units pay, at most` a IS
    `regular hours activity units pay` (`the units an activity earns` a)
        `the share of the monthly combined salary an activity unit is worth`
        `the most hours a month of section 3's longest week holds`

`section 21's units pay less than the law asks for a day out to 23:00 and for a night away` MEANS
        `the instrument pays less than the Hours of Work and Rest Law asks`
            (`regular hours section 16 asks for an escort day` 8 23)
            (`regular hours section 21's units pay, at most` (`an activity ending at` 23))
    AND `the instrument pays less than the Hours of Work and Rest Law asks`
            (`regular hours section 16 asks for the worked night away` FALSE)
            (`regular hours section 21's units pay, at most` (`an activity with nights away` 1))
#ASSERT `section 21's units pay less than the law asks for a day out to 23:00 and for a night away`

-- 4 units are 5.46 hours of a month of 195; 6 units, 8.19.
#ASSERT `regular hours section 21's units pay, at most` (`an activity ending at` 23) EQUALS 5.46
#ASSERT `regular hours section 21's units pay, at most` (`an activity with nights away` 1) EQUALS 8.19
